  "summary": "How the core gets a reactor thread to run a task (net/reactor.rs): Link::notify marks `dirty` once and pushes a Run message, Shared::send records a wake-up debt and pays it unless a hold is active, the release of a hold clears it and then pays, and the reactor sets `sleeping`, re-checks its queue, then polls; every published frame is taken without readiness, tick or timeout once the holds are released.",
